\description{
Runs the periodic steady state (\code{.pss}) of the circuit in \code{deck}, by
shooting--Newton: Newton on the period map \code{x(t0) -> x(t0 + T)} with
matrix-free GMRES, the Jacobian products by directional differences
over a frozen-grid replay of the period transient. A linear circuit
converges in one Newton step. The arguments are those of the card
\verb{.pss FREQ TSTAB OSCNODE POINTS HARMS SCITER STEADYCOEFF UIC}, and
the plots are, value for value, what that card gives in
\code{\link[=spice_run]{spice_run()}} -- the same engine call. The deck supplies the circuit
and its \code{.options}; its own analysis cards are not run.
}
\details{
The method is Dune's: ngspice-47's \code{.pss} is a free-running
oscillator search that detunes from a driving source. \code{points} is the
accuracy knob: the error left is the integrator's phase error,
\code{(2 * pi / points)^2 / 12} of the amplitude with the default
trapezoidal rule. Autonomous oscillators and transmission lines are
not supported yet.
}
